+/*
+ * Pose holds (peer-to-peer sessions only).  A game whose frame `frame` read
+ * something only a drawn picture of the state that frame starts from gives
+ * right ends its tick at that state instead, drawn, and plays the frames from
+ * `frame` again on the next.
+ *
+ * ggpo_can_hold_at: whether ggpo_hold_at(frame) could hold now: frame - 1's
+ * save is in the ring and every connected player's input for frame - 1 can
+ * still be read (queued, or predicted).  Read-only; may be called inside the
+ * advance_frame callback.  GGPO_OK, or INVALID_REQUEST.
+ *
+ * ggpo_hold_at: outside every callback, once the step's own calls are done:
+ * loads frame - 1's save and advances it once (load_game_state, then one
+ * advance_frame callback, as a rollback does), so the session stands at
+ * `frame`, and leaves the frames from `frame` up to the frame that was
+ * current to be played again (advance_frame callbacks, as a rollback's) first
+ * thing in the next ggpo_idle, ggpo_add_local_input or ggpo_disconnect_player,
+ * before anything is received; *frames_left gets how many.  Until then no
+ * other frame is loaded or advanced.  Called again before that replay (the
+ * replay of frame - 1 itself read such a thing), it holds further back and
+ * the frames left reach the same frame.  INVALID_REQUEST when it cannot:
+ * frame - 1 not kept, inside a callback, a misprediction not rolled back yet.
+ *
+ * So that a hold can replay from any saved frame, every input stays queued for
+ * as long as its frame's save is in the ring.
+ */
